.TH DLOAD 1.SH NAMEdload \- load a file as a data module.SH SYNOPSIS\fBdload\fRfile.SH DESCRIPTION\fBdload\fRreads a file and makes a data module in memory holding its contents,named after the file, so that other programs can link to it by name.  Itreports the size and where the module went:.nf    size of file is 10 bytes    datamodule created at address $   49034    done.fi.SH NOTESNeeds Microware's\fBcio\fR.\fR\fBunlink\fRremoves the module again..SH SEE ALSOsavemem, loadmem